NAME
    su - switch the active shell account

SYNOPSIS
    su [name]

DESCRIPTION
    Switches the current session's active account to <name>, or to
    'root' when <name> is omitted. The target account must already exist
    in the process account list (see useradd(1)). su does not prompt for
    a password.

    Sessions created with 'tmux new' inherit the active account of the
    current session rather than defaulting to root.

EXAMPLES
    su
    su guest

EXIT STATUS
    0   Switched to the requested account.
    1   Account does not exist.

SEE ALSO
    whoami(1), who(1), useradd(1), userdel(1), passwd(1), tmux(1)
